A||||7||mercurio||Fiero 84 Identification number ||||12||
Z||000000||mercurio||10-10-2001||06:55 PM||||i need to record my Fiero 84 according the federal rules on my country, i need to know where the identification number is on the car, i know that there is a label below the windscreen ,but on my car it is almost destroyed, do you know if there is another place, where i can find the identification number on my car?||||reg||12
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-10-2001||07:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mercurio:<BR><B>i need to record my Fiero 84 according the federal rules on my country, i need to know where the identification number is on the car, i know that there is a label below the windscreen ,but on my car it is almost destroyed, do you know if there is another place, where i can find the identification number on my car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It should be on the title...<BR>But if you don't get a title, then look in the front trunk area for a white sticker with all the codes, it may be on that, or on the sticker on the door jam...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||10-10-2001||07:22 PM||||Like Fierowrecker says it should appear on the white sticker inside the front trunk with the build codes on it. It will be the top item, a separate long combination of numbers and letters.  If you cannot find it here either, you may try taking apart the interior.  Stuffed in the dash, console, under panels and seats you may find slips of paper quoting the VIN number.  I found five or six in mine.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-10-2001||07:23 PM||||The VIN on the dash, lower left corner of winshield is a metal plate. Try folding a rag over a peice of sheet metal and scrub some of the junk off it.<P>There's a secondary plate. It's usually in the front compartment someplace. It may be hidden.<P>I think it's also on the white lable near the brake(and clutch) master cylinder(s). (On the fender.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||10-10-2001||09:05 PM||||where in mexico are you from? <BR><B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">   <BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||dman||10-10-2001||10:43 PM||||Hello everyone. <P>mercurio, if you can't find the white sticker on the drivers side front fenderwell, or the tag on the drivers door, there is one more place you can look.<P>Remove the drivers side speaker grill on the dash. I forget if you need to move the speaker but alongside or under the speaker is a secondary VIN plate.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||10-10-2001||11:10 PM||||On my 88 coupe I found old vin tags behind the radio, under drivers dash above petals. They were little tags about 1X2 inches. The glue had somewhat got hard and didnt stick well. I found them everywhere, I think one was under my shifter also...||||reg||12
Z||000007||Wolfhound||10-11-2001||08:00 AM||||Remove your drivers side dash speaker. Just below on a brace is a second VIN stamped into a brace. ||||reg||1
